# Line endings, kept the same everywhere on purpose.
#
# Three things here stop working silently if they get CRLF on a Windows
# checkout, and each of them cost an afternoon before this file existed. A
# patch under native/patches will not apply and, worse, will not be recognised
# as already applied, so the build fails on the second run rather than the
# first. A shell script under native/ is misread by bash a line at a time. And
# a C source rewritten with CRLF grows stray carriage returns in the middle of
# lines when anything edits it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one that genuinely wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Left alone.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.dic binary
